\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 1. Introduction\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield addresses the growing variety of phishing channels. A link-only tool is\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 useful but incomplete: attackers also rely on persuasive SMS messages, email bodies,\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 and images that imitate legitimate brands. CyberShield unifies these signals into a\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 single user-facing risk assessment while preserving the evidence needed for later\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 review.\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 1.1 Purpose\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 The purpose of this SRS is to define what CyberShield must do, its boundaries,\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 interfaces, data behavior, and quality attributes. It is written for developers, testers,\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 project reviewers, and future maintainers.\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 1.2 Scope\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 The system shall allow a registered or guest user to analyze a URL, text message, email\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 content, or screenshot. It shall identify suspicious indicators, assign a transparent risk\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 level, give safety guidance, retain records according to policy, and support\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 administrative oversight. It does not guarantee that every threat is detected or replace\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 organizational incident response.\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 1.3 Goals\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1  Detect common phishing indicators across web, text, and image inputs.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1  Explain findings in plain language without encouraging unsafe actions.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1  Protect submitted content, especially personally identifiable information.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1  Support continuous model and rule improvement using approved feedback.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Implementation Notes\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Implementation note: This requirement group is implemented through explicit\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 interfaces, versioned configuration, and measurable acceptance criteria. The design\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 keeps input validation, evidence collection, risk scoring, explanation, and audit\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 recording distinct so that a change in one component can be reviewed and tested\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 without unintentionally changing every result. Where uncertainty exists, the platform\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 states the limitation and provides a safe verification action instead of presenting a\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 binary assurance.\par
\page
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 1.4 Definitions, Acronyms, and Abbreviations\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Phishing: a deceptive attempt to obtain credentials, money, or sensitive information.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 URL: a web address. NLP: computational processing of natural-language text. IP:\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 image processing. OCR: optical character recognition. IOC: indicator of compromise.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Risk score: a normalized estimate used to classify an input as low, medium, high, or\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 critical risk.\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 1.5 References\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1  IEEE 830, recommended practice for software requirements specifications.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1  OWASP guidance on phishing, secure application design, and logging.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1  NIST SP 800-53 security and privacy controls; NIST guidance on incident response.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1  Project references: EXPIROCHAIN report structure and supplied SRS Formatting\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Guide.\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 1.6 Document Overview\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Section 2 describes the product context and users. Section 3 contains requirements for\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 each analysis mode, interfaces, quality attributes, and data. Section 4 provides system\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 models. The final sections define verification, operations, appendices, and references.\par
