\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 2. Overall Description\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 2.1 Product Perspective\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield is a web platform that coordinates a client interface, an application API, a\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 URL intelligence service, an NLP service, an image/OCR service, a risk-scoring\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 engine, and a protected data store. It can consume configurable reputation feeds and\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 may later integrate an organization\u8217?s security operations workflow.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 The product is a new multi-modal layer rather than a browser replacement, mail\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 gateway, or antivirus tool. It performs pre-action triage: it helps a user decide whether\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 to avoid, verify, report, or safely continue.\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 2.2 Product Functions\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1  Submit and normalize URLs for lexical, DNS/reputation, redirect, and\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 certificate-related checks.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1  Extract semantic and structural phishing cues from pasted SMS and email content.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1  Extract visible text and visual cues from screenshots using OCR and image analysis.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1  Fuse modality signals into an explainable classification and record an audit trail.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1  Present recommendations, feedback controls, administrative configuration, and\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 reports.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Implementation Notes\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Implementation note: This requirement group is implemented through explicit\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 interfaces, versioned configuration, and measurable acceptance criteria. The design\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 keeps input validation, evidence collection, risk scoring, explanation, and audit\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 recording distinct so that a change in one component can be reviewed and tested\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 without unintentionally changing every result. Where uncertainty exists, the platform\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 states the limitation and provides a safe verification action instead of presenting a\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 binary assurance.\par
\page
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 2.3 User Classes\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qc\b\fs22 Table 2: User Classes and Access\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Class\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Description\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Primary permissions\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Guest user\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Unregistered visitor\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Submit limited analyses; view current result only.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Registered user\par
